Now I understand the problem. The fix needs to be applied at line 304-306:

```js
if (this.reconnectAttempts >= maxAttempts) {
    this.emitter.emit("error", new Error(`Max reconnect attempts (${maxAttempts}) reached${options.code ? ` after code ${options.code}` : ""}`));
    this.monitor.destroy();
    return;
}
```

When `maxAttempts === 0` (shutdown path), `this.reconnectAttempts` is initially 0, so `0 >= 0` is true, causing an error to be emitted.

The fix should check if `maxAttempts === 0` first and emit a debug message instead:


Adding a debug log when max attempts is zero during shutdown, then emitting the error only when it's a legitimate failure scenario. Since I can't modify node_modules directly without breaking on reinstall, I should use patch-package to make this change persistent.

But wait—patch-package would alter node_modules which isn't ideal. Let me reconsider whether the project uses patches at all, or if there's a better approach like overriding the behavior in extensions/discord or elsewhere in the codebase.

